# Spot welding: a ceramic disc (C1) in the vise, its leads down; a
# second (C2) held flat, its lead 1 level, laid to C1's lead 2 6 mm from
# the body and welded by arm C's capacitor discharge, in the window of
# their copper-clad steel; then the LED (D1, a semiconductor) laid the
# same way to C1's lead 2 lower down. Welded as it is, the LED would take
# the discharge's transient, so the weld is refused: arm C takes the
# clip instead and clips the LED's lead to ground between its body and
# the lap, and arm B welds it. The tools back away and arm A lifts the
# three out of the vise as one.
reset circuit=weld
tool A tweezers
pick A C1 grasp=body
place A C1 at=0,0,-32
vise close
release A C1
pick A C2 grasp=body
move A to=0,40,10 rpy=-90,0,90
align A C2.1.tip to=C1.2.6 gap=0.1
tool C welder
weld C at=C1.2+C2.1 energy=8
release A C2
lift A mm=40
pick A D1 grasp=body
move A to=0,40,10 rpy=-90,0,90
align A D1.1.tip to=C1.2.13 gap=0.1
tool C clip
clip C on=D1.1 at=12
tool B welder
weld B at=C1.2+D1.1 energy=8
inspect C1.2+D1.1
back B mm=60
back C mm=60
release A D1
lift A mm=40
pick A C1 grasp=body
vise open
lift A mm=60
